        "a": 3,
        "e": "<strong>Physiological partitioning of postprandial glucose clearance (Topic 646):</strong> Comparing the quantitative metabolic data in Table 1 across the tissue-specific knockout models reveals the relative physiological contributions of muscle versus adipose tissue:<br>&bull; **Wild-Type Control:** Fasting glucose = 82.4 mg/dL; GTT AUC = 185.0 mg&middot;h/dL.<br>&bull; **Muscle-Specific KO (*MCK-Cre*):** Skeletal muscle GLUT4 is ablated (4.2% of WT) while adipose GLUT4 remains normal (98.4%). Fasting glucose climbs to 118.2 mg/dL, and the Glucose Tolerance Test AUC surges dramatically to **392.0 mg&middot;h/dL** (an increase of +112% over WT), approaching the severe intolerance of the global null (480.0 mg&middot;h/dL).<br>&bull; **Adipose-Specific KO (*Adipoq-Cre*):** Adipose GLUT4 is ablated (3.5% of WT) while muscle GLUT4 remains intact (97.8%). Fasting glucose is only mildly elevated (88.5 mg/dL), and GTT AUC shows only a minor increase to **224.0 mg&middot;h/dL** (+21% over WT).<br>Because selective ablation of GLUT4 in striated muscle reproduces the majority of the systemic glucose intolerance seen in global null mice, **skeletal muscle GLUT4-mediated uptake accounts for the dominant fraction (~70\u201380%) of postprandial glucose disposal in vivo**.<br><br><em>Distractor Traps:</em><br>&bull; A is contradicted by Table 1; Adipoq-Cre mice display only a mild increase in GTT AUC (224 vs 185 mg\u00b7h/dL) and near-normal fasting glucose (88.5 mg/dL).<br>&bull; B is contradicted by the MCK-Cre data; MCK-Cre ablates both skeletal muscle and myocardium GLUT4, whereas adipose-specific knockout preserves myocardium but neither demonstrates myocardial exclusivity.<br>&bull; C is contradicted by the data; muscle-specific knockout increases GTT AUC by 112% (to 392), whereas adipose knockout increases it by only 21% (to 224), proving non-equal contributions."
